Experiment - (a): Use date and who in a single command displaying date output on the screen and redirecting who output to a file.

Command: date; w | cat > who.txt
Explanation:
i) date : displays the current date and time on the screen.
ii) ; : separates two commands and executes them sequentially
iii) w : displays information about currently logged in users.
iv) | : pipe operator, passes the output of w to cat > who.txt
v) cat > who.txt : reads the input recieved from w and redirects the output in a file (who.txt).

Procedure :
1. Open the terminal.
2. Enter: date; w | cat > who.txt
3. Press enter.
4. The date and time are displayed on the screen.
5. The output of w is stored in who.txt.
6. To view the saved output, enter: cat who.txt.
Result : The date command output was displayed on the screen, while the output of the w command was successfully redirected and stored in who.txt.
